{
  "cells": [
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "# Chatbots \u2014 Rule-Based to Neural to LLM Agents Notebook\n\n> Hands-on Build It and Exercises."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "## Build It"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 1: rule-based pattern matching"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "import re"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        ""
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "class RulePattern:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    def __init__(self, pattern, response_template):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.regex = re.compile(pattern, re.IGNORECASE)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.template = response_template"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        ""
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "PATTERNS = ["
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    RulePattern(r\"my name is (\\w+)\", \"Nice to meet you, {0}.\"),"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    RulePattern(r\"i (need|want) (.+)\", \"Why do you {0} {1}?\"),"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    RulePattern(r\"i feel (.+)\", \"Why do you feel {0}?\"),"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    RulePattern(r\"(.*)\", \"Tell me more about that.\"),"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        ""
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def rule_based_respond(user_input):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    for pattern in PATTERNS:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        m = pattern.regex.match(user_input.strip())"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        if m:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            return pattern.template.format(*m.groups())"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return \"I don't understand.\""
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "ELIZA in 20 lines. The reflection trick (\"I feel sad\" \u2192 \"Why do you feel sad\") is the canonical psychotherapist demo from Weizenbaum 1966. Still instructive."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 2: retrieval-based (FAQ)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "This illustrative snippet requires `pip install sentence-transformers` (which pulls in torch). The runnable `code/main.py` for this lesson uses a stdlib Jaccard similarity instead, so the lesson runs without external dependencies."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "from sentence_transformers import SentenceTransformer"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "import numpy as np"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        ""
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "FAQ = ["
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    (\"how do i reset my password\", \"Go to Settings > Security > Reset Password.\"),"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    (\"how do i cancel my order\", \"Go to Orders, find the order, click Cancel.\"),"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    (\"what is your return policy\", \"30-day returns on unused items, original packaging.\"),"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        ""
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "encoder = SentenceTransformer(\"sentence-transformers/all-MiniLM-L6-v2\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "faq_questions = [q for q, _ in FAQ]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "faq_embeddings = encoder.encode(faq_questions, normalize_embeddings=True)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        ""
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def faq_respond(user_input, threshold=0.5):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    q_emb = encoder.encode([user_input], normalize_embeddings=True)[0]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    sims = faq_embeddings @ q_emb"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    best = int(np.argmax(sims))"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    if sims[best] < threshold:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        return None"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return FAQ[best][1]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Threshold-based refusal is the key design choice. If the best match is not close enough, return `None` and let the system escalate."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 3: neural generation (baseline)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Use a small instruction-tuned encoder-decoder (FLAN-T5) or a fine-tuned conversational model. Production-unusable on its own in 2026 (contradiction, off-topic drift, factual nonsense), but ships inside hybrid systems for natural phrasing. DialoGPT-style decoder-only models need explicit turn separators and EOS handling to produce coherent replies; a FLAN-T5 text2text pipeline works out of the box for a teaching example."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "from transformers import pipeline"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "chatbot = pipeline(\"text2text-generation\", model=\"google/flan-t5-small\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "response = chatbot(\"Respond politely to: Hi there!\", max_new_tokens=40)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "print(response[0][\"generated_text\"])"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 4: LLM agent loop"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "The 2026 production shape:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def agent_loop(user_message, tools, llm, max_steps=5):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    history = [{\"role\": \"user\", \"content\": user_message}]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    for _ in range(max_steps):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        response = llm(history, tools=tools)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        tool_call = response.get(\"tool_call\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        if tool_call:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            tool_name = tool_call.get(\"name\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            args = tool_call.get(\"arguments\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            if not isinstance(tool_name, str) or tool_name not in tools:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "                history.append({\"role\": \"assistant\", \"tool_call\": tool_call})"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "                history.append({\"role\": \"tool\", \"name\": str(tool_name), \"content\": f\"error: unknown tool {tool_name!r}\"})"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "                continue"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            if not isinstance(args, dict):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "                history.append({\"role\": \"assistant\", \"tool_call\": tool_call})"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "                history.append({\"role\": \"tool\", \"name\": tool_name, \"content\": f\"error: arguments must be a dict, got {type(args).__name__}\"})"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "                continue"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            fn = tools[tool_name]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            result = fn(**args)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            history.append({\"role\": \"assistant\", \"tool_call\": tool_call})"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            history.append({\"role\": \"tool\", \"name\": tool_name, \"content\": result})"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        else:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            return response[\"content\"]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return \"I could not complete the task in the step budget.\""
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Three things to name. Tools are callable functions the LLM can invoke. The loop terminates when the LLM returns a final answer instead of a tool call. The step budget prevents infinite loops on ambiguous tasks."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Real production adds: retrieval-first grounding (inject relevant docs before each LLM call), guardrails (refuse destructive actions without confirmation), observability (log every step), and evaluations (automated checks that agent behavior stays on-spec)."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 5: hybrid routing"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def hybrid_chat(user_input):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    if is_destructive_action(user_input):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        return structured_flow(user_input)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    faq_answer = faq_respond(user_input, threshold=0.6)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    if faq_answer:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        return faq_answer"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return agent_loop(user_input, tools, llm)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        ""
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def is_destructive_action(text):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    danger_words = [\"delete\", \"cancel\", \"charge\", \"refund\", \"transfer\"]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return any(w in text.lower() for w in danger_words)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "The pattern: deterministic rules for anything destructive, retrieval for canned FAQs, LLM agents for everything else. This is what ships in 2026 customer-support systems."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "## Exercises"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "1. **Easy.** Implement the rule-based respond above with 10 patterns for a coffee-shop ordering bot. Test edge cases: double orders, modifications, cancellation, unclear intent.\n2. **Medium.** Build a hybrid FAQ + LLM fallback. 50 canned FAQ entries for a SaaS product, LLM fallback with retrieval over the docs site. Measure refusal rate and accuracy on 100 real support questions.\n3. **Hard.** Implement the agent loop above with three tools (search, read-user-data, send-email). Run an evaluation with 50 test scenarios including prompt injection attempts. Report off-task rate, failed task rate, and any injection success."
      ]
    }
